  "goodToKnow": "Der Rohbau is the shell of a building: walls, floors and roof structure without interior finishing. When the roof frame is complete, builders celebrate the Richtfest, with a small tree or wreath on top and a speech by the carpenter. After the Rohbau comes der Innenausbau. Figuratively, a plan im Rohbau is in rough form. Roh means raw. Plural: die Rohbauten."
